        "lengthAssumptions": [
          "A length is the field's standard length: characters for A, digits before the decimal point for N and P (the n of n.d; the d digits follow it), and bytes for every other format.",
          "One byte per A character in a single-byte EBCDIC code page; U is UTF-16 (two bytes per character), so its character limit is half its length.",
          "N is zoned decimal, one byte per digit; P is packed decimal, (digits ÷ 2) + 1 bytes with the sign in the last nibble.",
          "D is a Natural date and T a Natural time, stored packed (4 and 7 bytes); B, I, F and L take their stated length in bytes.",
